  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on the 22nd February 2005, the proposed single storey detached outbuilding at the end of the rear garden of 4 Avenue Crescent, Hounslow is not lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.\r\n\r\nREASON:  The development does not fall within Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995, because the site is located within the Cranford Village Conservation Area (Article 1(5) Land), and as such the provision, alteration or improvement of a building with a cubic content greater than 10m? is not permitted."
